-- title:
--   The standard cyclic smooth-sieve majorant satisfies linear-forms pseudorandomness
-- statement:
--   For every length $k\ge3$ and error $\eta>0$, there is a natural primorial cutoff $w$ covering the exceptional primes of the full CFZ affine-form family such that, for all sufficiently large $M$, the standard smooth cyclic Selberg majorant at modulus $M+1$ and sieve level $\operatorname{sieveLevel}(k,M+1)$ satisfies the $k$-linear-forms condition with error $\eta$, simultaneously for every reduced residue modulo $\operatorname{primorial}(w)$.
